<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (Task 3 - Customer Engagement: 73.99% of consumer-months are Highly Engaged, 25.57% Moderately, and 0.44% Disengaged. Despite this, 58.54% of spend still flows through offline POS vs. 41.47% through digital channels. Recency and frequency differentiate engagement most strongly \(Disengaged: 19.7 inactive days vs. near-zero for engaged groups\). A relative threshold \(bottom 20% engagement among Healthy customers\) identifies a practical target of 75 customers \(7.51%\), since a strict absolute definition yields only 1.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 285 0 R
/E (Task 4 - Customer Segmentation: K-Means clustering \(k = 4, silhouette = 0.312\) covers 100% of the 999 - customer base: Healthy & Highly Engaged \(49.4%\), Stretched but Highly Engaged \(41.6%\), Emerging Digital \(8.4%\), New & Early-Dormant \(0.5%\). The Stretched segment holds 54 of the 59 Danger Zone customers identified in Task 2.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
